title Standfast -- the apostrophe convention becomes a check, and 129 fragile witness claims read natively
prompt Kyri, read the canon and the card, take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, Standfast on reds first, send often
think Standfast before new work. Walked crux/REDS.md for open agent-closable reds and found #85 marked CLOSED on 20260817 with the claim that the loom now guarded the class.
think Measurement beats memory, so I grepped the whole tools/ surface for the banned shape rather than trusting the closure note. 21 HUNK witnesses still carried it -- 126 sites of `printf '%s' '${out}' | grep -q` plus three more interpolating a different captured variable.
think The prior sweep was real and honest for the 97 image_* witnesses; what it never had was a mechanical check. A convention lives only where a reader remembers it, so a template written before the rule kept seeding fragile checks forward. That is the root, one layer above the sites.
think Verified the 126 sites were one uniform shape before touching them -- every `let X = run [...grep...]` paired with `assert (trim X.out) == "yes" else "MSG"`, zero mismatches -- so the conversion could be exact rather than approximate.
think Converted all 129 to one honest line each: `assert out contains "PHRASE" else "MSG"`, reading the captured string in the interpreter where an apostrophe is only a letter.
think Ran seven of the converted witnesses GREEN on metal rather than re-reading the diffs -- a conversion that compiles is not a conversion that holds.
think Built the loom so the class can never re-enter: a scan enforcing zero captured-output interpolations inside shell quotes across every runnable tools/*.rish, with two ratchets reported honestly rather than pretended away.
think The first cut of the guard was too wide and fired on a path interpolation in the key-generation script -- a false positive. Tightened it to the exact hazard class (a captured `.out` quoted into a shell word) and demoted the wider printf-into-grep shape to an advisory report.
think Proved both RED paths on metal: the tracked fragile control caught by prove-red, and a fragile line planted in a real witness making the enforce leg name that file by path and refuse.
obs The honest correction is that a fix can convince its own author. The 20260817 note read the class as guarded because the sweep it ran was thorough within its own family; the HUNK family simply was never in view. Recorded as a reopening that points back rather than a quiet edit.
obs Two ratchets stay named rather than swept blind. The four device-gated host scripts (HAWM adb/Seva, SETU hearth carry, TUBE install proof) want a phone or an outer terminal to witness, so converting them from the jail would be an unproven claim. The wider shape in waymark_derive is structurally safe -- a derived four-letter word cannot carry an apostrophe -- so it is debt rather than a red.
obs Appending the reopening note pushed crux/REDS.md past its 24576-byte bound, exactly the drift REDS #87 taught. Folded the five oldest closed prose notes (73, 74, 75, 78, 80) to crux/archive/ under the same closed-range discipline as the four folds before it -- every byte kept.
obs Rota item 22 read this lap: context/SILO_TECHNIQUE.md.
loom witness=witness_claim_check_witness sites_converted=129 witnesses_converted=21 enforce_files=1663 advisory_device_gated_sites=10 advisory_shape_sites=8
loom green_on_metal=7 witnesses=hunk_artifact,hunk_scroll_cursor,hunk_session_list,hunk_preset_shelf,hunk_scroll_fling,hunk_sprite_store,hunk_sprite_shelf
loom reds_bytes_before=26136 reds_bytes_after=22138 bound=24576 notes_folded=5
file tools/witness_claim_check_witness.rish the loom -- every runnable witness reads its own claim natively, both RED paths proven
file tools/fixtures/witness_claim_check_scan.sh the scan behind it -- enforce roster, two advisory ratchets, prove-red mode
file tools/fixtures/witness_claim_check_control/fragile_control.rish the planted fragile control, deliberately wrong so prove-red keeps proving
file crux/REDS.md REDS #85 reopened and closed with a check standing behind the claim; folded back under bound
file crux/archive/REDS-closed-prose-notes-73-80.md the closed prose notes lifted whole, nothing removed
file crux/REMEMBER.md the Now line refilled with this lap's lesson
recommend keep-going -- the Microkernel Target crux waits: a supervision loop that spawns its children FROM a roster and refuses a spawn the declaration never granted. No key, no funds.
